  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\n## SCE in Nephrology Blueprint\n\nCandidates are tested on a wide range of common and important disorders as set\n\nThe composition of the paper is as follows:\n\nTopic\n\n## Total\n\n| Topic Glomerulonephritis, tubulointerstitial nephritis                                               |   Number of questions* 30 |\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------|\n| Acute kidney injury; acute renal replacement therapy; disorders of fluid; electrolytes and acid base |                        26 |\n| Chronic kidney disease, haematuria; proteinuria                                                      |                        24 |\n| Renal bone disease, renal anaemia                                                                    |                        12 |\n| Cardiovascular disease, hypertension; renovascular disease and diabetes                              |                        20 |\n| Urological presentations including renal stone disease; urinary tract infection and obstruction      |                        14 |\n| Inherited and rarer diseases                                                                         |                        14 |\n| Peritoneal dialysis                                                                                  |                         8 |\n| Haemodialysis                                                                                        |                        14 |\n| Renal transplantation                                                                                |                        14 |\n| Other^                                                                                               |                        24 |\n\nNumber of questions*\n\n200\n\nThe questions in each category are distributed across both papers\n\nThis should be taken as an indication of the likely number of questions the actual number may vary.\n\n'Other' includes the following topics:\n\n- [ ] Therapeutics &amp; safe prescribing\n\n- [ ] Practical procedures\n\n- [ ] Renal disorders in pregnancy\n\n- [ ] Sexual health\n\n- [ ] Infection in the renal patient\n\n- [ ] Adult-paediatric interface\n\n- [ ] Active supportive (non-dialysis) care\n\n- [ ] End-of-life care MP\n\n- [ ] Nutrition\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nRCPE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## MRCP(UK) Central Office\n\n11 St Andrews Place Regent's Park London NW1 4LE\n\nTel: +44 (0)20 3075 1515\n\nwww.mrcpuk.org",
